<title>POLAND: Poland sells PLN 189 mln of fixed bonds.</title>
<headline>Poland sells PLN 189 mln of fixed bonds.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland sold 189 million zlotys of 12-percent fixed bonds due on June 12, 2001, after investors bid for 245 million, the central bank said.</p>
<p>The minimum price of the bonds was 81.00 and the average price was 81.18. Full details about the auction is on  NBPV.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 2 653 9700</p>
